id: 4
hanzi: 摸
pinyin: mō
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to touch; to stroke; to feel with hands; to grope for; to fathom or probe
  es: tocar; palpar; acariciar; tantear; buscar a tientas; sondear o averiguar

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to physically place hands or fingers upon an object to perceive texture, temperature, or shape; to feel or stroke | palpar o poner la mano sobre un objeto para percibir su textura, temperatura o contorno; tocar | 摸摸额头 (feel one's forehead)
  2 | Verb | Standard | to probe, fathom, search out, or ascertain an underlying situation or regular pattern | sondear, averiguar o descifrar a tientas una situación, pauta o ánimo | 摸清底细 (fathom the real background)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 母亲伸出手轻轻摸了摸孩子的额头，确定他烧已经退了，这才欣慰地松了一口气。 | Mǔqīn shēnchū shǒu qīngqīng mō le mō háizi de étóu, quèdìng tā shāo yǐjīng tuì le, zhè cái xīnwèi de sōng le yì kǒuqì. | The mother reached out and gently felt the child's forehead, and relieved to confirm his fever had subsided, she breathed a sigh of ease. | La madre extendió la mano y palpó con ternura la frente del niño; al comprobar que la fiebre había remitido, suspiró aliviada.
  #2 | 经过深入细致的实地调研，团队终于摸清了当地消费市场的真实需求与潜在增长点。 | Jīngguò shēnrù xìzhì de shídì diàoyán, tuánduì zhōngyú mōqīng le dāngdì xiāofèi shìchǎng de zhēnshí xūqiú yǔ qiánzài zēngzhǎngdiǎn. | Following thorough and meticulous field research, the team finally fathomed the local market's genuine consumer demands and potential growth avenues. | Tras minuciosas pesquisas sobre el terreno, el equipo logró al fin sondear y clarificar las auténticas demandas de los consumidores locales y sus nichos de expansión.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  摸摸头 | stroke or pat someone's head
  摸索规律 | fumble for and discover regular patterns
  摸清底细 | ascertain the real facts; probe bottom lines
  盲人摸象 | blind men feeling an elephant
  捉摸不定 | unpredictable; elusive to grasp
  摸黑前行 | grope forward in the dark

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  盲人摸象 | máng rén mō xiàng | blind men feeling an elephant; taking a part for the whole
  难以捉摸 | nán yǐ zhuō mō | hard to fathom; unpredictable; elusive
  摸爬滚打 | mō pá gǔn dǎ | go through arduous trials and grueling practice
  偷偷摸摸 | tōu tōu mō mō | surreptitious; sneaky; underhanded

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  摸 | mō | touch; feel with hand; grope | tocar; palpar; tantear | 扌 | hand | 扌 (hand, tactile probing) | 莫 (mò, sunset dusk / absence of light) | 13 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: hand radical 扌 indicates tactile physical contact, while 莫 (dusk / searching when the sun sinks into grass) conveys groping in dimness. | When darkness falls across the grass (莫), one stretches out a gentle hand (扌) to feel and grope one's way along (摸). | Al caer la penumbra entre los pastos (莫), la mano (扌) se extiende prudente tanteando el sendero a ciegas (摸). | 55 | QTAK | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: In the absence of sunlight (莫), you must stretch out your hands (扌) to touch and grope your way forward (摸).
  composite_memory_hook_es: En la penumbra cuando el sol declina (莫), la mano (扌) se alarga para tocar y tantear el camino (摸).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: The character 摸 merges physical haptic exploration with mental conjecture. In Chinese cognitive metaphor, 'feeling an object with hands' (触觉) directly maps onto 'fathoming intangible human motives or systemic laws' (摸底, 摸索, 捉摸).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'mō' (55). Pronounced with an even, sustained, clear acoustic pitch contour.

traps_and_cognates:
