semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 摸 stresses tactile exploration through hands and fingers, or figurative probing to ascertain unknown circumstances.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 摸 vs. 碰 | pèng | 摸 involves deliberate, continuous manual rubbing or feeling to assess texture, whereas 碰 denotes a brief, abrupt collision or casual contact (碰见, 碰杯).
    2 | 摸 vs. 抓 | zhuā | 摸 is gentle, exploratory, and sensory (palping surface texture), whereas 抓 is a forceful, grasping action using curled fingers to seize or clutch an object firmly.
    3 | 摸 vs. 摸索 | mōsuǒ | 摸 is the direct monosyllabic physical verb (摸额头), while 摸索 is an abstract disyllabic verb emphasizing painstaking, trial-and-error exploration over time to overcome unfamiliar challenges.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 穿过幽暗曲折的长廊，他只能伸出双手在潮湿的石壁上小心摸索。指尖触碰到的冰冷岩石凹凸不平，隐约传来的微弱风声指引着前进的方向。在黑暗中慢慢摸索，每一步都充满对未知的敬畏。 | Chuānguò yōu'àn qūzhé de chángláng, tā zhǐ néng shēnchū shuāngshǒu zài cháoshī de shíbì shàng xiǎoxīn mōsuǒ. Zhǐjiān chùpèng dào de bīnglěng yánshí āotū-bùpíng, yǐnyuē chuánlái de wēiruò fēngshēng zhǐyǐn zhe qiánjìn de fāngxiàng. Zài hēi'àn zhōng mànmàn mōsuǒ, měi yí bù dōu chōngmǎn duì wèizhī de jìngwèi. | Traversing the dim, winding corridor, he could only extend both hands to carefully grope along the damp stone wall. The cold, jagged rock touched by his fingertips and faint breezes hinted at the path ahead. Fumbling patiently in the dark, every step was fraught with awe toward the unknown. | Cruzando el oscuro y tortuoso corredor, no le quedaba más remedio que alargar las manos y tantear la húmeda pared de roca. El tacto gélido y desigual de la piedra y el leve rumor de una corriente guiaron sus pasos. Avanzar a tientas en las sombras colmaba cada pisada de respeto hacia lo ignoto.
  #2 | 任何新兴科学领域的探索，初期都宛如盲人摸象，科学家们只能凭借有限的实验数据逐步摸清其内在逻辑。唯有汇聚多学科的智慧并进行反复验证，才能拼凑出客观规律的完整图景。 | Rènhé xīnxīng kēxué lǐngyù de tànsuǒ, chūqī dōu wǎnrú mángrén mō xiàng, kēxuéjiāmen zhǐ néng píngjiè yǒuxiàn de shíyàn shùjù zhúbù mōqīng qí nèizài luóji. Wéiyǒu huìjù duō-kēxué de zhìhuì bìng jìnxíng fǎnfù yànzhèng, cáinéng pīncòu chū kèguān guīlǜ de wánzhěng tújǐng. | Explorations into emergent scientific fields initially resemble blind men feeling an elephant; researchers must deduce intrinsic mechanisms through limited experimental data. Only by pooling interdisciplinary wisdom and reiterating tests can a coherent panorama of objective laws be pieced together. | Explorar una disciplina científica incipiente se asemeja al tanteo de los ciegos ante el elefante: los científicos infieren la lógica subyacente con escasos datos empíricos. Solo combinando múltiples ramas del saber y verificando hipótesis se logra reconstruir la fisonomía íntegra de la realidad objetiva.
